[1m[38;2;0;191;255mPURPOSE[0m
[38;5;252mJørgen 2026-11-19 08:55Z: attach a request to a piece of the text in a mark mode, so the AI knows [39m
[38;5;252mexactly what it is about; questions today look like acceptance criteria. 09:05Z (answer 1 on this [39m
[38;5;252mtask): threads inside the ticket would bloat it, and the conversation must not become the thing.  [39m
[38;5;252mThe ticket must stay crisp: clarity comes from boiling text down to its essence. The messy part   [39m
[38;5;252mgoes to a separate, suitably named history file in the task's files (provenance, chat history)    [39m
[38;5;252mthat grows by appending.                                                                          [39m

[1m[38;2;0;191;255mPRINCIPLE[0m
[38;5;252mTicket = working document, short and current. History = append-only provenance file, linked from  [39m
[38;5;252mthe ticket, never needed to understand the ticket. Marks are plain text in the field they are     [39m
[38;5;252mabout, so git, grep, any editor and any agent see them. Resolving a mark means changing the       [39m
[38;5;252mticket, not adding to it. The agent instruction: lead with clarity in the ticket, answer and act  [39m
[38;5;252mon marks, post new questions as marks, move the dialogue to history. Reuse an existing markup     [39m
[38;5;252mconvention for the sigil if one fits. Either side may resolve a mark (Jørgen 09:05Z): the person  [39m
